WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.285
Welcome to One DSD People, Access and Culture.
Whether you're a director, manager, supervisor,

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.205
or staff member, this is a place to

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.525
connect equity with your everyday work.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.765
You can build understanding, prepare for a
decision, or find a useful resource.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.100
Learning here is voluntary. Start where you are,
and explore at your own pace.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.675
Choose Enter One DSD to reach the home

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.155
page. Begin with a question from your work,

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:31.995
then explore learning, practical tools, or
support. You can go directly to a resource,

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.915
follow a learning path, or return to something

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.470
you have already started. There is no required
order.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.435
Connect learning with work helps you choose a

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.815
starting point: build your understanding, work

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:51.255
through a decision, or examine what helped. The
program connects learning, practice, and

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.435
reflection. Choose the starting point that fits

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:57.010
your responsibility and return as your question
develops.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.515
For disability services work, explore DSD

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.595
programs and services. Find a relevant service,

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.735
then open Equity question and resources. These
connections help you consider the people

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.795
involved, possible barriers, and useful

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.555
guidance. DSD sits within the Aging and

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.955
Disability Services Administration, or ADSA.
Keep your own responsibilities and the relevant

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.750
requirements in view.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:30.815
In Learning and resources, search for a question

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:36.015
or choose a theme. Foundation, Intermediate, and
Advanced describe learning depth, not your job

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:38.015
title. Look for what a course helps you

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.255
practice and prepare. You can explore team

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.835
collaboration, policy work, communication, and

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:46.330
other topics, choosing what is useful for the
work ahead.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.995
The library brings courses, practical guidance,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.255
books, and recordings together. Search for a

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.215
topic or follow a theme.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.775
Where a podcast or short reading is available,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.275
choose whether to listen or read the

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.735
accompanying words. You can pause and return to

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.630
a passage. Listening is optional.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.455
Books and ideas for your work offers two

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.835
hundred readings in nine collections.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.755
Search by title, author, or idea, or choose

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.855
a reading path. Each reading includes a summary,

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:27.975
key ideas, and questions. Compare perspectives,
discuss a question, and follow connections into

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.755
practice. These are authors’ perspectives, not

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.450
agency policy.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.295
To see the wider purpose, open People, Access

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:45.315
and Culture in practice from the home page. The
first video introduces the Equity Outcome

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.315
Map. The second follows DSD examples connected

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.915
to the six ADSA goals. Beside the examples,
links show which existing

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.750
tools can help you take the next step.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.055
The Equity Analysis Toolkit helps you examine a

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:07.455
decision. Consider who is affected, what the
evidence supports, and which alternatives

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.995
deserve attention. Open Practice with the

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.515
toolkit to watch a worked example, explore the

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:17.215
completed responses, and try a separate
situation. Use the questions to prepare your own

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.450
draft for the appropriate review.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.215
Resources can help you prepare thoughtful

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:31.435
questions. Minnesota Communities offers context,
and the cultural and language-access guidance

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:35.635
helps you consider participation. Use them
alongside conversations with the people

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.335
affected. A resource cannot tell you what every

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:43.230
person needs, and a prepared analysis does not
replace the responsible decision-maker.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:52.335
My work helps you return to saved resources and
plans. Use the same browser and device,

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.055
and check the saving message on each activity.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.815
Download a copy when needed. Keep private client
and personnel information

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:01.015
out of learning notes. For a question needing

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.690
an official response, use Find the right person
or office.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.295
Begin with one question, one useful resource,

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.995
and one step you can try. Notice what changed
and whose experience still

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.155
needs attention. Return to this User guide

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.215
whenever you need directions. The written guide

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.750
includes links and a download so you can find
your way again.
